// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 16 (Impl-U, Cohort Delta): the Tier-O
// classification — E2's honest fallback (W2C §1.1/§38). A value with
// no tier-classified origin (an int here; an unannotated extern's
// results identically — P2's default-unpure opaque form) is
// classified O: no delta-local law at any price. The delta record
// kind on O values is a checked refusal; the tape falls back to
// OPAQUE (kind 0) — the record kinds are tier-parametric.
fn main() {
    tape<int> t = tape_new("o")
    int x = 5
    tape_record(t, 1, x, x)
}
